[center][b][size=4][youtube]xfCIAxEiWr0[/youtube][/size][/b][/center]

Makes Far Cry 2 sound like a serious shooter: real reverb, new gun sounds, echoes and gunfire echoes.

[size=4][b]What it changes[/b][/size]
[list]
[*][b]Reverb is back.[/b] The game always had it, but it only played on old sound cards. Now every building sounds like its size, and the jungle, savannah and desert each sound different.[/*]
[*][b]Walls muffle the outside[/b] depending on what they're made of. Open doors and windows let the sound in.[/*]
[*][b]New gunshots[/b] for almost every weapon. Full-auto plays a shot for every round.[/*]
[*][b]Echoes[/b] after every unsuppressed shot, yours and the enemy's.[/*]
[*][b]Distant gunfire cracks[/b] instead of just getting quieter.[/*]
[*][b]New explosions[/b] for grenades and rockets, close and far.[/*]
[*][b]Voices fade out with distance[/b] instead of carrying across a whole camp.[/*]
[*][b]No more distant dogs and jackals[/b] in the background. Every other animal stays.[/*]
[*][b]A rougher engine idle[/b] for the Datsun pickup.[/*]
[*][b]Combat music can be turned off[/b], so you can hear the enemy in a fight. Calm music still plays. Find it in [b]Options → Mod Configuration Menu[/b].[/*]
[/list]

[size=4][b]How to install (Vortex)[/b][/size]

[list=1]
[*]Install [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/about/vortex/]Vortex[/url] and its Far Cry 2 extension.[/*]
[*]Click [b]Mod Manager Download[/b] on this page and enable the mod. Vortex also offers to get [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/farcry2/mods/368]FCSE[/url], which this mod needs.[/*]
[*]Start the game with the [b]Play[/b] button in Vortex.[/*]
[/list]
Not using Vortex? Install it with JackAll instead, [url=https://jbebe.github.io/farcry-sdk/jackall/installing-mods/]here's a detailed instruction[/url] for JackAll installation.

[size=4][b]Good to know[/b][/size]
[list]
[*][b]Needs Far Cry 2 patch 1.03[/b], Steam or GOG, and FCSE 1.4.0 or later.[/*]
[*][b]Remove any [font=Courier New]dsound.dll[/font] already in your game's [font=Courier New]bin[/font] folder.[/b] It clashes with this mod.[/*]
[*][b]It's a good idea to install Sound Overhaul first, then individual weapons second so that they can override the sounds.[/b][/*]
[/list]

[size=4][b]Credits[/b][/size]
[list]
[*]Gunshots, echoes and explosions: [b]Dark Signal Weapon Soundscape[/b] (DSWS), by Dark Signal's original producer, with assets from [b]JSRS[/b].[/*]
[*][url=https://github.com/kcat/dsoal]DSOAL[/url] and [url=https://github.com/kcat/openal-soft]OpenAL Soft[/url], by Chris Robinson, under the LGPL-2.1. Their licenses ship beside them in the download.[/*]
[/list]
